--
-- V2 — reference data. Generated by scripts/build-new-baseline.sh.
--
-- V1 creates the tables and nothing else, so platform.applications and
-- platform.queues arrive empty. Almost everything has a foreign key onto one
-- of them: a workflow names an application, a binding names a queue, an event
-- names the application that publishes it. Without these rows the seeds fail
-- and nothing can be authored.
--
-- No tenant owns any of this. It is the same in every environment, which is
-- what makes it safe to ship as a migration rather than as someone's setup
-- notes.
--
-- Organisations and users are NOT here. They are yours to create, and seeding
-- a fake one is how a fake one reaches production.
--
-- Written by the database itself with format(%L), not by rewriting a pg_dump
-- with sed. The sed version silently produced `INSERT INTO ) ON CONFLICT` for
-- every row, because --column-inserts spans lines and the pattern ate them.
--
-- SAFE TO RE-RUN.
--

